                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "With the release of the remake \"Amerzone - The Explorer's Legacy (2025)\", this original version was given out for Free!\n\nThis game was the first work made in together by the established French developers Microids and the Belgian comic artist Benoit Sokal, which became the birth place of the entire SYBERIA series.\n\nThe remake looks astonishingly beautiful and is on my radar, but first I wanted to experience the original, especially after having completed all the Syberia games.\nThe setting and atmosphere are very similar if not the same. Now that I finished the game, I remember various Amerzone easter-eggs in the Syberia games. Nice.\n\nThis retro game looked very good for its time, yet was a bit too short and difficult for players back then.\nOnly due to winning an award it got the attention that propelled the game's success.\nTo think if it failed, Microids wouldn't have worked with B.Sokal and we wouldn't have Syberia..\n\nThe graphics and the animations are nice.\nMusic and sound were a standout (don't know why people complained about back then.)\nThe written texts were immersive but a bit too much, especially the damn cursive handwriting.\nPuzzles were not that hard, but some pixel hunting/hotspots were annoying. (chapter 1 lift)\nOverall the game is worth checking out for its meaningful lesson and beautiful journey.\n\n\nBUT what killed this game for me, was the damn SOFT LOCK at the VERY END OF THE GAME!!!\nI don't care if a game is perfect and I like it,\nif it is a broken product that soft locks the player then it instantly goes on my Blacklist!\n-\nSo you go through this whole journey and place the egg in the perfect egg spot and the game just won't let you progress! APPARENTLY you have to find a dark cave which is very hard to see, heat up the egg there and only then put it in the egg spot. How many players did make this innocent mistake?!?\nYou mean to say since 1999 players had to suffer through this soft lock??\nSure back then, devs could not patch a sold disk! But come the f on, we are in digital era, and this game is on Steam!\n\"Amerzone 1999\" was released on STEAM on August 22, 2014. it has been here for 12 years now!\nYou mean to tell me Microids didn't have the time to release a TINY patch??\nMODDERS RELEASE FAN PATCHES, you mean to tell me Microids don't give a flying fk?!?\nNah, this is unforgivable.\nI didn't have a save and wasn't going to replay half the game, so I watched the last 5 minutes of gameplay on a Youtube Walkthrough.\nThanks, Microids. Thank you so much for cucking your fans.\n\n\nThis is a good game, but how can I recommend it to my peers who will step on the same landmine?\nUnless they fix it, this will remain a negative rating.",
